,"yearOfPublication":2016,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Sci Data","title":"Scientific data","essn":"2052-4463","issn":"2052-4463","isoabbreviation":"Sci Data","nlmid":"101640192"},"printPublicationDate":"2016-03-01"},"pubYear":"2016","pageInfo":"160018","abstractText":"There is an urgent need to improve the infrastructure supporting the reuse of scholarly data. A diverse set of stakeholders-representing academia, industry, funding agencies, and scholarly publishers-have come together to design and jointly endorse a concise and measureable set of principles that we refer to as the FAIR Data Principles. The intent is that these may act as a guideline for those wishing to enhance the reusability of their data holdings. Distinct from peer initiatives that focus on the human scholar, the FAIR Principles put specific emphasis on enhancing the ability of machines to automatically find and use the data, in addition to supporting its reuse by individuals. This Comment is the first formal publication of the FAIR Principles, and includes the rationale behind them, and some exemplar implementations in the community.","affiliation":"Center for Plant Biotechnology and Genomics, Universidad Politécnica de Madrid, Madrid 28223, Spain.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["article-commentary","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council","acronym":"BB_","grantId":"BB/H024921/1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council","acronym":"BB_","grantId":"BB/J020265/1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Economic and Social Research Council","grantId":"ES/L007487/1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIDDK NIH HHS","acronym":"DK","grantId":"U24 DK097771","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIDA NIH HHS","acronym":"DA","grantId":"U24 DA039832","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council","acronym":"BB_","grantId":"BB/E025080/1",